<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olaf Guthfrithson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 941</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olaf Guthfrithson was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> from 934 and of York from 939 until his death in 941. In 937 he led the Dublin Norse in alliance with the Scots and the Britons of Strathclyde against King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Æthelstan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunanburh">Battle of Brunanburh</a>. After Æthelstan's death he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> and the Five Boroughs, but he died soon afterwards.</p></div>
